sp.p:
I don't, so help me—grudge it him a bit, though I'm as good as he;
                               but I hates this here expense, when such a lot of us are out o'
                               work, and hungry. That's all I've got to say.

My good people, what need is there of all this irrational violence;
                                you may hear me speak any other day to the same effect. I now
                                propose to make an address to Time.
